<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE FROM MONDAY.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE FROM MONDAY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Friday it will cut its retail price for diesel in the Netherlands by two cents per litre with effect from November 4.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. Gasoline prices will remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Monday the recommended price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations goes down to 1.50 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
